## Worksheet

**F1 — Core loop**: `Game` class holds all state; `mulberry32(seed)` seeds `this.rng`, used throughout `initMap`, `endTurn`, `fireEvent`; `endTurn()` resolves consumption→morale→production→skills→departures→caravan→storm→events→caps→win/lose in fixed order. Score: 2

**F2 — Map**: 8x8 loop builds `this.map`; terrain via `this.rng()`; `buildBuilding` checks `building_def.terrain.includes(tile.terrain)`; no adjacency-bonus code anywhere. Score: 1

**F3 — Economy**: `ore_forge` consumes power→metal, `greenhouse`/`hydro_farm` consume water→food; storage caps enforced with overflow logged; but no real 2-hop chain (e.g. ore→metal→tool). Score: 1

**F4 — Population**: colonists have skill/fatigue/morale/job, but `produceResources()` uses hardcoded `avg_skill = b.workers>0?3:1`, and `assigned_building`/`workers` are never set anywhere. Score: 1

**F5 — Needs**: `food_need`/`water_need` consumed, deficits decrement `col.morale`; but `produceResources()` never reads `col.morale`, and morale never increases (no recovery). Score: 1

**F6 — Research**: 8 nodes, prereqs checked in `completeResearch`, costs deducted; `buildBuilding` gates on research for 7/8 nodes, but `repair` node (`unlocks:null`) has zero effect anywhere. Score: 1

**F7 — Events**: only 7 events defined (`event_defs`), below the 10+ requirement; 6 have differing 2-choice outcomes; `events_fired` cooldown check exists. Score: 1

**F8 — Trade**: `tradeResource` buy/sell both work; price reads `market_demand` which is initialized to 0 and never updated anywhere; no caravan inventory cap. Score: 1

**F9 — Hazard**: `storm_arrival` countdown, severity `turn/10`; `applyAshstorm` sets `tile.building.damage`; `produceResources` applies `damage_factor`; `storm_shelter` (research-gated) reduces damage; `repairBuilding` spends parts and restores output. Score: 2

**F10 — Save/load**: `save()` serializes state to JSON in textarea via `saveGame()`; `load()` uses try/catch JSON.parse, `loadGame()` alerts clear error on failure. Score: 2

**F11 — End conditions**: lose at `colonists.length===0`; win at `turn>=60 && pop>=12 && food/water thresholds` (reachable via visitor events); `endGame` computes multi-factor `total_score`; `showEndGame` renders breakdown modal. Score: 2

**F12 — UI**: `switchTab` wired to buttons; log entries show `[T${entry.turn}]`; keydown listener for Space/1-5; media query adapts layout; `.tooltip`/`.tooltip-text` CSS defined but never applied to any element. Score: 1

**F13 — Dev panel**: `runTests()` checks 15 real invariants (caps, prereqs, PRNG determinism, save/load roundtrip, bounds); `runBenchmark()` runs 200 headless `endTurn()` calls and prints `simpleHash(final_state)`. Score: 2

**G1**: `buildBuilding` reads `research[building_def.research].completed` to gate 5 output-producing buildings; production formula uses their `output_base` once unlocked — indirect gate, not a live yield multiplier. Score: 3

**G2**: `food_deficit`/`water_deficit` write `col.morale -=1`, but `produceResources()` never reads `col.morale` — chain breaks at final link. Score: 1

**G3**: `applyAshstorm` sets `tile.building.damage`; `produceResources` applies `damage_factor`; `repairBuilding` spends 5 parts, reduces damage, restoring output; shown in UI (`dmg` class, damage%). Score: 4

**G4**: price formula reads `market_demand[resource]` but that object is never mutated anywhere after construction — always 0, no real responsiveness to stockpile or supply. Score: 0

**G5**: `discovery` choices differ (parts+10 vs scrip+5); `accident`/`visitor` choices each write distinct resource/colonist mutations, not just log lines. Score: 4

